{"content_hash": "54a94d1d3ff9b6fb", "version_id": 755, "article_id": 76, "level_code": "en_c1", "lang": "en", "level": 5, "level_label": "C1 高级", "title": "Meta cuts deal with Zuckerberg to cover his wealth tax", "title_zh": "Meta和扎克伯格达成协议，帮他交富豪税", "has_translation": true, "topic": "tech", "source": "guardian_tech", "source_url": "https://www.theguardian.com/technology/2026/oct/22/meta-mark-zuckerberg-california-wealth-tax", "image": {"type": "photo", "url": "https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1689439518196-f48a24b49fb5?ixid=M3wxMDk3Mzk1fDB8MXxzZWFyY2h8Mnx8bWV0YSUyMHN0cmlrZXMlMjBkZWFsfGVufDB8MHx8fDE3OTI3OTk4NTF8MA&ixlib=rb-4.1.0&w=1600&q=75&fm=jpg&fit=max", "provider": "unsplash", "credit": "Photo by Julio Lopez on Unsplash", "author": "Julio Lopez", "credit_url": "https://unsplash.com/@juliolopez?utm_source=daily-english-news&utm_medium=referral", "source": "Unsplash", "source_url": "https://unsplash.com/photos/a-person-holding-up-a-cell-phone-in-front-of-a-sign-ilbjfRwOgzA?utm_source=daily-english-news&utm_medium=referral", "fallback": {"type": "gradient", "from": "hsl(112, 42%, 62%)", "to": "hsl(150, 46%, 48%)", "label": "TECH", "seed": "ba10886f1e8e"}}, "published_date": "2026-10-24", "word_count": 283, "reading_minutes": 1.4, "lead": "Meta has agreed to issue new shares to its chief executive so he can pay a possible California billionaire tax — provided he stays in the state for eight years. The move comes as voters prepare to decide on the measure.", "lead_zh": "Meta同意向自家CEO发放新股，好让他有钱交加州可能开征的富豪税——条件是他在加州再住八年。此时正值选民即将对该提案投票。", "preview": "The social media group behind Facebook, Instagram and WhatsApp disclosed on Wednesday night that the arrangement would keep Mark Zuckerberg ", "preview_zh": "旗下拥有Facebook、Instagram和WhatsApp的这家社交媒体集团周三晚间披露，这一安排将让马克·扎克伯格继续居住在Meta总部所在的加州。根据条款，他将获得一批新股，一旦加州通过对富豪一次性征税的提案，这些股票可被出售以支付数十亿美元的税单。作为交换，他承诺在未来", "has_audio": true, "audio": {"id": 743, "url": "https://pub-aba43a6fb1db4dc08fede1dbc81f3241.r2.dev/audio/76/en_c1.mp3", "duration": 116.825, "size_bytes": 701856, "engine": "kokoro", "voice": "af_heart", "word_count": 334, "has_timeline": true, "alternates": [{"voice": "af_bella", "url": "https://pub-aba43a6fb1db4dc08fede1dbc81f3241.r2.dev/audio/76/en_c1_af_bella.mp3", "duration": 119.25, "size_bytes": 716400, "engine": "kokoro", "word_count": 334, "has_timeline": true, "timeline_url": "https://pub-aba43a6fb1db4dc08fede1dbc81f3241.r2.dev/timeline/76/en_c1_af_bella.json"}, {"voice": "am_michael", "url": "https://pub-aba43a6fb1db4dc08fede1dbc81f3241.r2.dev/audio/76/en_c1_am_michael.mp3", "duration": 127.825, "size_bytes": 767952, "engine": "kokoro", "word_count": 334, "has_timeline": true, "timeline_url": "https://pub-aba43a6fb1db4dc08fede1dbc81f3241.r2.dev/timeline/76/en_c1_am_michael.json"}, {"voice": "bf_emma", "url": "https://pub-aba43a6fb1db4dc08fede1dbc81f3241.r2.dev/audio/76/en_c1_bf_emma.mp3", "duration": 110.475, "size_bytes": 663840, "engine": "kokoro", "word_count": 334, "has_timeline": true, "timeline_url": "https://pub-aba43a6fb1db4dc08fede1dbc81f3241.r2.dev/timeline/76/en_c1_bf_emma.json"}, {"voice": "bm_george", "url": "https://pub-aba43a6fb1db4dc08fede1dbc81f3241.r2.dev/audio/76/en_c1_bm_george.mp3", "duration": 119.825, "size_bytes": 719856, "engine": "kokoro", "word_count": 334, "has_timeline": true, "timeline_url": "https://pub-aba43a6fb1db4dc08fede1dbc81f3241.r2.dev/timeline/76/en_c1_bm_george.json"}]}, "detail_url": "https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/chjam12301-sys/news-etl@5eaba37/content/data/versions/755.json", "paragraphs": ["The social media group behind Facebook, Instagram and WhatsApp disclosed on Wednesday night that the arrangement would keep Mark Zuckerberg resident in California, where Meta is headquartered. Under the terms, he will receive new shares that could be sold to settle a multibillion-dollar bill should California pass a one-off levy on billionaires. In exchange, he has pledged to remain a resident of the state, or wherever Meta keeps its base, for eight years.", "Californians vote early next month on Proposition 40, a one-off 5% tax on the roughly 250 billionaires living in the state. Zuckerberg, whose fortune Forbes puts at $239bn, told Meta he was weighing a move elsewhere, since the measure could expose him to a huge liability and potentially force him to sell voting shares. Meta's response is a two-for-one stock split creating a new class of non-voting shares, letting him cash out without loosening his grip on the company.", "Polling suggests Prop 40 still lacks majority support. Tech billionaires, among them Sergey Brin, Peter Thiel and Eric Schmidt, have spent heavily to defeat it. Congressman Rohit Khanna framed the vote as a choice between the working class and the oligarchs, arguing that \"every society is taxed. The only question is who will pay.\"", "Meta also reported a 26% rise in quarterly revenue to $64.6bn, beating forecasts, though profits fell 37% to $13bn after a $9.9bn charge tied to lawsuits over child protection and social media addiction. Shares slid more than 6% at Thursday's open, dragging the Nasdaq down 2.5%. Separately, a New Mexico judge ordered Meta to pay $25bn for misleading the public over Facebook user data, and the company said headcount had fallen 15% year on year to 66,775."], "paragraphs_zh": ["旗下拥有Facebook、Instagram和WhatsApp的这家社交媒体集团周三晚间披露，这一安排将让马克·扎克伯格继续居住在Meta总部所在的加州。根据条款，他将获得一批新股，一旦加州通过对富豪一次性征税的提案，这些股票可被出售以支付数十亿美元的税单。作为交换，他承诺在未来八年内继续居住在加州，或Meta设总部的地方。", "加州选民下月初将就第40号提案投票，该提案对居住在加州的约250名亿万富翁一次性征收5%的税。据《福布斯》估算身家2390亿美元的扎克伯格告诉Meta，他正考虑搬离，因为该提案可能让他背上巨额税负，甚至被迫出售有投票权的股票。Meta的应对是进行二比一的拆股，创设一类无投票权的新股，让他能套现而不削弱对公司的掌控。", "民调显示，第40号提案仍未获得多数支持。包括谢尔盖·布林、彼得·蒂尔和埃里克·施密特在内的科技亿万富翁已投入巨资反对该提案。国会议员罗希特·卡纳把这次投票描述为在工人阶级与寡头之间做选择，并称“每个社会都要征税，问题只在于谁来付”。", "Meta还公布季度营收增长26%至646亿美元，超出预期，但利润下滑37%至130亿美元，原因是与儿童保护和社交媒体成瘾相关诉讼有关的99亿美元费用。周四开盘后股价下跌逾6%，拖累纳斯达克指数下跌2.5%。另外，新墨西哥州一名法官裁定Meta因在Facebook用户数据问题上误导公众而须支付250亿美元，公司还表示员工人数同比减少15%，降至66775人。"], "body": "The social media group behind Facebook, Instagram and WhatsApp disclosed on Wednesday night that the arrangement would keep Mark Zuckerberg resident in California, where Meta is headquartered. Under the terms, he will receive new shares that could be sold to settle a multibillion-dollar bill should California pass a one-off levy on billionaires. In exchange, he has pledged to remain a resident of the state, or wherever Meta keeps its base, for eight years.\n\nCalifornians vote early next month on Proposition 40, a one-off 5% tax on the roughly 250 billionaires living in the state. Zuckerberg, whose fortune Forbes puts at $239bn, told Meta he was weighing a move elsewhere, since the measure could expose him to a huge liability and potentially force him to sell voting shares. Meta's response is a two-for-one stock split creating a new class of non-voting shares, letting him cash out without loosening his grip on the company.\n\nPolling suggests Prop 40 still lacks majority support. Tech billionaires, among them Sergey Brin, Peter Thiel and Eric Schmidt, have spent heavily to defeat it. Congressman Rohit Khanna framed the vote as a choice between the working class and the oligarchs, arguing that \"every society is taxed. The only question is who will pay.\"\n\nMeta also reported a 26% rise in quarterly revenue to $64.6bn, beating forecasts, though profits fell 37% to $13bn after a $9.9bn charge tied to lawsuits over child protection and social media addiction. Shares slid more than 6% at Thursday's open, dragging the Nasdaq down 2.5%. Separately, a New Mexico judge ordered Meta to pay $25bn for misleading the public over Facebook user data, and the company said headcount had fallen 15% year on year to 66,775.", "body_zh": "旗下拥有Facebook、Instagram和WhatsApp的这家社交媒体集团周三晚间披露，这一安排将让马克·扎克伯格继续居住在Meta总部所在的加州。根据条款，他将获得一批新股，一旦加州通过对富豪一次性征税的提案，这些股票可被出售以支付数十亿美元的税单。作为交换，他承诺在未来八年内继续居住在加州，或Meta设总部的地方。\n\n加州选民下月初将就第40号提案投票，该提案对居住在加州的约250名亿万富翁一次性征收5%的税。据《福布斯》估算身家2390亿美元的扎克伯格告诉Meta，他正考虑搬离，因为该提案可能让他背上巨额税负，甚至被迫出售有投票权的股票。Meta的应对是进行二比一的拆股，创设一类无投票权的新股，让他能套现而不削弱对公司的掌控。\n\n民调显示，第40号提案仍未获得多数支持。包括谢尔盖·布林、彼得·蒂尔和埃里克·施密特在内的科技亿万富翁已投入巨资反对该提案。国会议员罗希特·卡纳把这次投票描述为在工人阶级与寡头之间做选择，并称“每个社会都要征税，问题只在于谁来付”。\n\nMeta还公布季度营收增长26%至646亿美元，超出预期，但利润下滑37%至130亿美元，原因是与儿童保护和社交媒体成瘾相关诉讼有关的99亿美元费用。周四开盘后股价下跌逾6%，拖累纳斯达克指数下跌2.5%。另外，新墨西哥州一名法官裁定Meta因在Facebook用户数据问题上误导公众而须支付250亿美元，公司还表示员工人数同比减少15%，降至66775人。", "text": "The social media group behind Facebook, Instagram and WhatsApp disclosed on Wednesday night that the arrangement would keep Mark Zuckerberg resident in California, where Meta is headquartered. Under the terms, he will receive new shares that could be sold to settle a multibillion-dollar bill should California pass a one-off levy on billionaires. In exchange, he has pledged to remain a resident of the state, or wherever Meta keeps its base, for eight years. Californians vote early next month on Proposition 40, a one-off 5% tax on the roughly 250 billionaires living in the state. Zuckerberg, whose fortune Forbes puts at $239bn, told Meta he was weighing a move elsewhere, since the measure could expose him to a huge liability and potentially force him to sell voting shares. Meta's response is a two-for-one stock split creating a new class of non-voting shares, letting him cash out without loosening his grip on the company. Polling suggests Prop 40 still lacks majority support. Tech billionaires, among them Sergey Brin, Peter Thiel and Eric Schmidt, have spent heavily to defeat it. Congressman Rohit Khanna framed the vote as a choice between the working class and the oligarchs, arguing that \"every society is taxed. The only question is who will pay.\" Meta also reported a 26% rise in quarterly revenue to $64.6bn, beating forecasts, though profits fell 37% to $13bn after a $9.9bn charge tied to lawsuits over child protection and social media addiction. Shares slid more than 6% at Thursday's open, dragging the Nasdaq down 2.5%. Separately, a New Mexico judge ordered Meta to pay $25bn for misleading the public over Facebook user data, and the company said headcount had fallen 15% year on year to 66,775.", "vocab": [{"word": "strike a deal", "pos": "phrase", "zh": "达成协议", "note": "比 make a deal 更正式，新闻常用", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "foot the bill", "pos": "phrase", "zh": "买单，付账", "note": "常指替别人承担费用", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "levy", "pos": "noun", "zh": "征税，税款", "note": "one-off levy 指一次性征税", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "one-off", "pos": "adj", "zh": "一次性的", "note": "英式表达，美式常用 one-time", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "disclose", "pos": "verb", "zh": "披露，公开", "note": "比 reveal 更正式，多用于公司公告", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "headquartered", "pos": "adj", "zh": "总部位于……的", "note": "be headquartered in 某地", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "liability", "pos": "noun", "zh": "债务，法律责任", "note": "税务语境指应缴税款", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "weigh", "pos": "verb", "zh": "权衡，考虑", "note": "weigh a move 考虑搬迁", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "stock split", "pos": "phrase", "zh": "拆股", "note": "two-for-one 指一拆二", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "dilute", "pos": "verb", "zh": "稀释（股权）", "note": "dilute control 削弱控制权", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "loosen one's grip", "pos": "phrase", "zh": "放松控制", "note": "形象说法，指失去掌控", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "lack majority support", "pos": "phrase", "zh": "缺乏多数支持", "note": "民调常用搭配", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "frame", "pos": "verb", "zh": "把……描述为", "note": "frame A as B 把A说成B", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "drag down", "pos": "phrase", "zh": "拖累，拉低", "note": "常用于股指、股价", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}], "fetched_at": "2026-10-23T23:57:30.310630", "timeline": [{"i": 0, "w": "The", "s": 0.25, "e": 0.362, "sm": 250, "em": 362, "cs": 0, "ce": 3, "si": 0}, {"i": 1, "w": "social", "s": 0.362, "e": 0.75, "sm": 362, "em": 750, "cs": 4, "ce": 10, "si": 0}, {"i": 2, "w": "media", "s": 0.75, "e": 1.075, "sm": 750, "em": 1074, "cs": 11, "ce": 16, "si": 0}, {"i": 3, "w": "group", "s": 1.075, "e": 1.35, "sm": 1075, "em": 1